# Renault Megane III five-door hatchback, 2009-2016.
#
# The third-generation Megane in its pre-facelift form (2008-2012), on sale in
# Britain from 2009 and replaced in the summer of 2016 by the Megane IV, whose
# European production began that year.
# https://www.renault.co.uk/ (Megane III model page, cited in the reference pack)
#
# Dimensions 4.295 x 1.808 x 1.471 m, wheelbase 2.641 m. Source: the reference
# pack's notes. The hull measures 4.295 m on a 2.641 m wheelbase (61.5 per
# cent) and 1.808 m wide; mirrors take it to 2.050 m.
#
# Shape reference: all three photographs are of the same silver five-door, and
# image 1 is a true level side elevation, matched directly. The model's central
# window pillar is more steeply raked than the photograph and the hatch
# treatment is simplified, but the side window band, wheel positions and roof
# line agree. All glazing panes stand 10-20 mm clear of the local body surface.
#
# Note from the research pack: British-market five-door hatches were built at
# Bursa in Turkey, with roof weather strips covering the welds and a slightly
# higher ride height than the Spanish-built cars; the model follows the
# photographed car.
#
# Colours are from a Renault UK brochure of November 2011, evidence grade (a),
# with the caveat that the list is printed for the Coupe edition and the hatch
# used the same palette family: Glacier White, Pacific Blue, Capsicum Red,
# Stone, Extreme Blue, Ruby Red, Oyster Grey, Chestnut Brown, Mercury, Eclipse,
# Diamond Black, Cayenne and Malta Blue. Four are modelled: Glacier White,
# Pacific Blue, Capsicum Red and Oyster Grey. Weights white 3, blue 3, red 2,
# grey 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 190 km/h, the 1.6-litre turbo's quoted maximum. Comfort 100/480, on the
# line 330 + 1.5 x 100: a quiet, well-finished family hatchback. Classes 0,1.
#
# Dates are road presence: 2009 intro, retires staggered 2024-2027 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/renault-megane-iii.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/renault-megane-iii.dae (65 objects). References:
# citycars/references/renault-megane-iii/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the central window pillar is too steeply raked and the
# headlamp and rear hatch treatment simplified. At 128 px the rounded nose, the
# rising waistline and the gently falling roof read as the Megane III.

obj=citycar
